; SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later

; =============================================================================
; ComboboxCtl — measured against @base-ui/react/combobox
; =============================================================================
; A text box that filters a listbox, and — with `multiple` on — the same box
; holding its selection as CHIPS beside the caret, each with a remove button.
; That is the M-Files metadata card's lookup field ("ESTT Corporation ×" with
; a caret beside it) and its class picker, and it was the one component the
; plan had declined twice for want of an oracle: "a tag input is genuinely new,
; and the interesting part is what Backspace does at position 0".
;
; Radix has neither. Base UI ships both as one component, so the oracle is
; conformance/oracle/combobox_oracle.mjs and the numbers it wrote are in
; combobox.json. Everything below that says "measured" is a line in that file.
;
; --- THE SHAPE, MEASURED ------------------------------------------------------
;
;   input     role COMBOBOX, aria-haspopup=listbox, aria-autocomplete=list,
;             aria-expanded — and it is the ONE tab stop. The trigger and the
;             clear button are tabindex=-1, and so is every chip: a keyboard
;             reaches all of them from the input.
;   trigger   a button that opens the list; focus stays on the input.
;   clear     a button that is ABSENT until there is a value. Not disabled:
;             gone from the tree.
;   chips     role TOOLBAR. A chip carries no role and its label as its name;
;             the remove inside it is a button named "Remove <label>".
;   list      role LISTBOX, aria-multiselectable="true" when `multiple`; the
;             rows are OPTIONs with aria-selected following the SELECTION and
;             not the highlight — which is the opposite of Radix's select, and
;             is why this file does not share SelectCtl's rows.
;
; --- OPENING, MEASURED ---------------------------------------------------------
;
;   A click on the input opens the list; so does the trigger; so does a click
;   on a chip. When something is chosen, the highlight lands ON IT; when
;   nothing is, a click leaves NO highlight and ArrowDown puts it on the first
;   row. Arrows move the highlight and never the value.
;
; --- CHOOSING, MEASURED --------------------------------------------------------
;
;   Single: Enter or a click on the highlighted row takes its label into the
;   input, closes the list and leaves focus in the input. Multiple: the same
;   gesture TOGGLES the row, the list STAYS OPEN and the highlight stays where
;   it was — three picks are three keystrokes. Chips are appended in the order
;   they were picked, not the order of the list.
;
; --- TYPING, MEASURED ----------------------------------------------------------
;
;   Typing filters the list (case-insensitive contains, Base UI's default) and
;   CLEARS the highlight — there is no autoHighlight, so "ru" then Enter
;   chooses nothing: the list closes and the box REVERTS to the chosen label.
;   Nothing matching draws the Empty text. Focus leaving a box that holds a
;   partial or a nonsense query reverts it too; leaving a box that was emptied
;   clears the selection. A multiple box's query is cleared instead of reverted,
;   because its selection is in the chips and the box never held a label.
;
; --- THE CHIPS, MEASURED -------------------------------------------------------
;
;   Backspace in an EMPTY input removes the LAST chip — it does not focus it
;   first — and, because Backspace is typing, the list opens. ArrowLeft in an
;   empty input closes the list and moves focus onto the last chip; ArrowLeft
;   again walks back along them; ArrowLeft past the first WRAPS to the input.
;   Backspace or Delete on a focused chip removes it and focus goes to the
;   chip now in its place — or the one before it when it was the last — and to
;   the input when none remain. Enter on a chip goes back to the input. The
;   remove button removes its chip and focus goes to the input.
;
; --- SPECIFIED, NOT MEASURED ---------------------------------------------------
;
;   ArrowRight from a chip (the mirror of ArrowLeft, ending on the input),
;   ArrowUp on a closed list (opens it on the last row), and whether a
;   multiple pick clears the typed query (it does here — the measured Enter
;   with a query pending cleared it, and a pick is the same commitment). Each
;   is a rule the harness could not reach; none of them is a guess about ARIA.
;
; --- AUTOCOMPLETE MODE (`autocomplete` on) --------------------------------------
;
;   Base UI's Autocomplete (and ReUI's, built on it): the same input, list and
;   keys, but the TEXT is the value and the list only offers to complete it.
;   Written from Base UI's documented Autocomplete and the WAI-ARIA combobox
;   pattern with list autocomplete; not yet a line in combobox.json.
;
;     * Nothing is ever "chosen": no revert on blur, no revert on an Enter with
;       nothing highlighted, and `aria-selected` marks the highlighted row
;       (the APG's listbox-autocomplete rule) rather than a selection.
;     * A click in the box does not open the list (openOnInputClick is off);
;       typing does, and ArrowDown / ArrowUp do. Emptying the box closes it.
;     * Enter or a click on a row puts its label into the box and closes.
;       Escape closes; Escape on a closed box with text clears it (as the
;       single combobox above). Tab closes and accepts nothing.
;     * `inlineComplete` (aria-autocomplete="both", Base UI mode="both"): a
;       keystroke that GROWS the text highlights the first row whose label
;       starts with it and writes that label's remaining letters after the
;       caret, selected — the next letter types over them, Backspace removes
;       them. The arrows show the highlighted row's whole label; Escape and
;       Tab put back what was typed.
;     * Optional: section headings (`addGroupedItem`, role=group rows labelled
;       by their heading), a `limit` with a "N more" line, a `loading` state,
;       the matching part of each label as its own run (`emphasis`), and no
;       trigger or no clear button (`showTrigger`, `showClear`).
;
; --- OPT-IN OPTIONS, EITHER MODE (off by default) ---------------------------
;
;   From Base UI's documented Combobox, not from combobox.json: `hoverHighlight`
;   (the pointer over a row highlights it, as the autocomplete always does),
;   `loopFocus` (an arrow past either end takes the highlight back to the
;   input and the next one wraps — Base UI's default; the measured hosts keep
;   the stop at the ends) and `showClear` false (no Combobox.Clear part).
; =============================================================================

Import "UiCtl.rgr"
Import "UiTree.rgr"
Import "InputCtl.rgr"
Import "pkg:evg/EVGElement.rgr"
Import "pkg:evg/EVGA11yTree.rgr"

class ComboboxCtl extends UiCtl {
    ; One value in the box, or many as chips.
    def multiple:boolean false
    def items:[UiItem]
    ; The chosen value when single, "" for none.
    def value:string ""
    ; The chosen values when multiple, in the order they were picked.
    def values:[string]
    def open:boolean false
    ; The highlighted option — where Enter lands — "" for none. Not the value:
    ; measured, the arrows move this and only Enter or a click moves that.
    def activeValue:string ""
    ; The chip holding focus, "" while focus is in the input.
    def chipFocus:string ""
    ; Is the input's text a QUERY, typed since the list opened, or the chosen
    ; label? Decides what the list shows and what a blur does.
    def filtering:boolean false
    def placeholder:string ""
    def emptyText:string "No results."
    ; `aria-required` and `aria-invalid`, handed down from a Field.
    def required:boolean false
    def invalid:boolean false
    ; --- autocomplete mode: see the header. All off by default. ---
    def autocomplete:boolean false
    def inlineComplete:boolean false
    def showTrigger:boolean true
    def showClear:boolean true
    ; --- combobox options, off by default (the measured behaviour) ---
    ; The pointer over a row highlights it, as Base UI's Combobox does; the
    ; measured hosts (form, metadata) route no hover, so it is opt-in.
    def hoverHighlight:boolean false
    ; Base UI's `loopFocus`: an arrow past the last (or first) row takes the
    ; highlight back to the input, and the next one onto the other end.
    def loopFocus:boolean false
    def emphasis:boolean false
    ; At most this many rows (0: all), and a line saying how many more match.
    def limit:int 0
    def moreSuffix:string " more — keep typing to narrow"
    def loading:boolean false
    def loadingText:string "Loading…"
    ; What the person TYPED — the query — apart from an inline completion
    ; shown after it.
    def typed:string ""
    ; Each item's section heading, parallel to `items`; "" for none.
    def itemGroups:[string]
    def moreEl:EVGElement
    def loadingEl:EVGElement
    ; The text box. Its caret, selection and word motion are InputCtl's nine
    ; specs; this class only decides what its text MEANS.
    def input:InputCtl
    def groupEl:EVGElement
    def chipsEl:EVGElement
    def clearEl:EVGElement
    def triggerEl:EVGElement
    def contentEl:EVGElement
    def emptyEl:EVGElement

    Constructor () {
        rootEl = (EVGElement.createDiv())
        groupEl = (EVGElement.createDiv())
        chipsEl = (EVGElement.createDiv())
        clearEl = (EVGElement.createDiv())
        triggerEl = (EVGElement.createDiv())
        contentEl = (EVGElement.createDiv())
        emptyEl = (EVGElement.createDiv())
        input = (new InputCtl())
        def empty:[UiItem]
        items = empty
        def none:[string]
        values = none
        def noGroups:[string]
        itemGroups = noGroups
        moreEl = (EVGElement.createDiv())
        loadingEl = (EVGElement.createDiv())
    }

    fn addItem:void (itemValue:string itemName:string itemDisabled:boolean) {
        def it (new UiItem())
        it.value = itemValue
        it.name = itemName
        it.disabled = itemDisabled
        push items it
        push itemGroups ""
    }

    ; An item under a section heading. Items of one section are added together;
    ; the heading is drawn above the first of them that the filter lets through.
    fn addGroupedItem:void (itemValue:string itemName:string group:string) {
        this.addItem(itemValue itemName false)
        def last:int ((array_length itemGroups) - 1)
        set itemGroups last group
    }

    ; Every item gone — a host that fetches its suggestions replaces them.
    fn clearItems:void () {
        def empty:[UiItem]
        items = empty
        def noGroups:[string]
        itemGroups = noGroups
        activeValue = ""
    }

    fn groupOf:string (v:string) {
        def i:int (this.indexOfValue(v))
        if ((i < 0) || (i >= (array_length itemGroups))) {
            return ""
        }
        return (itemAt itemGroups i)
    }

    ; A section's id: its position among the sections, so a heading with
    ; spaces in it makes a clean id.
    fn sectionTid:string (group:string) {
        def seen:[string]
        def i:int 0
        while (i < (array_length itemGroups)) {
            def g:string (itemAt itemGroups i)
            if ((strlen g) > 0) {
                if ((indexOf seen g) < 0) {
                    push seen g
                }
            }
            i = (i + 1)
        }
        return (tid + "-section-" + (to_string (indexOf seen group)))
    }

    fn sectionLabelTid:string (group:string) {
        return ((this.sectionTid(group)) + "-label")
    }

    fn moreTid:string () {
        return (tid + "-more")
    }

    fn loadingTid:string () {
        return (tid + "-loading")
    }

    ; --- ids ----------------------------------------------------------------------

    fn inputTid:string () {
        return (tid + "-input")
    }

    fn triggerTid:string () {
        return (tid + "-trigger")
    }

    fn clearTid:string () {
        return (tid + "-clear")
    }

    fn chipsTid:string () {
        return (tid + "-chips")
    }

    fn chipTid:string (v:string) {
        return ((tid + "-chip-") + v)
    }

    fn chipRemoveTid:string (v:string) {
        return (((tid + "-chip-") + v) + "-remove")
    }

    fn contentTid:string () {
        return (tid + "-content")
    }

    fn emptyTid:string () {
        return (tid + "-empty")
    }

    ; The option the highlight is on while the list is open, "" otherwise —
    ; what the input's `aria-activedescendant` names. Not `aria-selected`,
    ; which follows the selection (see `rows`).
    fn activeOptionTid:string () {
        if (open == false) {
            return ""
        }
        if ((strlen activeValue) == 0) {
            return ""
        }
        return (this.itemTid(activeValue))
    }

    fn itemTid:string (v:string) {
        return ((tid + "-item-") + v)
    }

    ; --- lookups ------------------------------------------------------------------

    fn indexOfValue:int (v:string) {
        def i:int 0
        while (i < (array_length items)) {
            def it:UiItem (itemAt items i)
            if (it.value == v) {
                return i
            }
            i = (i + 1)
        }
        return -1
    }

    fn labelOf:string (v:string) {
        def i:int (this.indexOfValue(v))
        if (i < 0) {
            return ""
        }
        def it:UiItem (itemAt items i)
        return it.name
    }

    fn isChosen:boolean (v:string) {
        if autocomplete {
            return false
        }
        if multiple {
            return ((indexOf values v) >= 0)
        }
        return (v == value)
    }

    ; The option a target names, "" when it is not one.
    fn itemValueOf:string (target:string) {
        def i:int 0
        while (i < (array_length items)) {
            def it:UiItem (itemAt items i)
            if (target == (this.itemTid(it.value))) {
                return it.value
            }
            i = (i + 1)
        }
        return ""
    }

    ; The chip a target names — the chip itself, or its remove button.
    fn chipValueOf:string (target:string) {
        def i:int 0
        while (i < (array_length values)) {
            def v:string (itemAt values i)
            if (target == (this.chipTid(v))) {
                return v
            }
            i = (i + 1)
        }
        return ""
    }

    fn chipRemoveValueOf:string (target:string) {
        def i:int 0
        while (i < (array_length values)) {
            def v:string (itemAt values i)
            if (target == (this.chipRemoveTid(v))) {
                return v
            }
            i = (i + 1)
        }
        return ""
    }

    ; The typed query, or "" when the box holds a label rather than a filter.
    fn query:string () {
        if autocomplete {
            return typed
        }
        if filtering {
            return input.value
        }
        return ""
    }

    ; Case-insensitive CONTAINS — Base UI's default filter. Measured only as
    ; far as "ru" matching Ruby and Rust and "ty" matching TypeScript alone,
    ; which a prefix match would also pass; the choice between the two is the
    ; reference's documented default rather than a capture.
    fn matches:boolean (it:UiItem q:string) {
        if ((strlen q) == 0) {
            return true
        }
        def hay:string (to_lowercase it.name)
        def needle:string (to_lowercase q)
        return ((indexOf hay needle) >= 0)
    }

    ; The rows the list shows now: what the query lets through, cut to
    ; `limit`, and none while a fetch is pending.
    fn visibleItems:[UiItem] () {
        def all:[UiItem] (this.matchedItems())
        def out:[UiItem]
        if (autocomplete && loading) {
            return out
        }
        if ((limit <= 0) || ((array_length all) <= limit)) {
            return all
        }
        def i:int 0
        while (i < limit) {
            push out (itemAt all i)
            i = (i + 1)
        }
        return out
    }

    ; How many matching rows the limit left out.
    fn hiddenCount:int () {
        if (autocomplete && loading) {
            return 0
        }
        if (limit <= 0) {
            return 0
        }
        def n:int (array_length (this.matchedItems()))
        if (n <= limit) {
            return 0
        }
        return (n - limit)
    }

    ; Everything the query lets through.
    fn matchedItems:[UiItem] () {
        def out:[UiItem]
        def q:string (this.query())
        def i:int 0
        while (i < (array_length items)) {
            def it:UiItem (itemAt items i)
            if (this.matches(it q)) {
                push out it
            }
            i = (i + 1)
        }
        return out
    }

    fn visibleIndexOf:int (vis:[UiItem] v:string) {
        def i:int 0
        while (i < (array_length vis)) {
            def it:UiItem (itemAt vis i)
            if (it.value == v) {
                return i
            }
            i = (i + 1)
        }
        return -1
    }

    fn stateWord:string () {
        if open {
            return "open"
        }
        return "closed"
    }

    ; Is the clear button in the tree? It follows the TEXT, not the value:
    ; measured, emptying the box with Backspace removed it before anything had
    ; been committed, and a half-typed query kept it. A multiple box never has
    ; one — its chips carry their own.
    fn showsClear:boolean () {
        if autocomplete {
            return (showClear && ((strlen input.value) > 0))
        }
        if multiple {
            return false
        }
        ; `showClear` off: a box drawn without Base UI's Combobox.Clear part.
        return (showClear && ((strlen input.value) > 0))
    }

    ; What the box shows when nothing is being typed: the chosen label, or
    ; nothing at all for a multiple box, whose choices are its chips.
    fn restingText:string () {
        if multiple {
            return ""
        }
        return (this.labelOf(value))
    }

    ; Put the resting text back and drop the query.
    fn settleText:void () {
        filtering = false
        input.setValue((this.restingText()))
        input.caret = (strlen input.value)
        input.anchor = input.caret
    }

    ; --- opening and closing ------------------------------------------------------

    ; Open with the highlight on what is chosen — measured: the chosen row,
    ; the first chosen for a multiple box, and none when nothing is.
    fn openOnChosen:string () {
        open = true
        activeValue = ""
        if multiple {
            if ((array_length values) > 0) {
                activeValue = (itemAt values 0)
            }
        } {
            activeValue = value
        }
        this.build()
        return (this.inputTid())
    }

    fn closeList:void () {
        open = false
        activeValue = ""
        this.settleText()
        this.build()
    }

    ; --- choosing -----------------------------------------------------------------

    fn choose:string (v:string) {
        def i:int (this.indexOfValue(v))
        if (i < 0) {
            return ""
        }
        def it:UiItem (itemAt items i)
        if it.disabled {
            return ""
        }
        if multiple {
            ; TOGGLE, stay open, keep the highlight where it is. Measured.
            def at:int (indexOf values v)
            if (at >= 0) {
                remove_index values at
            } {
                push values v
            }
            activeValue = v
            ; The query is spent: see the header's "specified, not measured".
            filtering = false
            input.setValue("")
            input.caret = 0
            input.anchor = 0
            this.build()
            return (this.inputTid())
        }
        value = v
        open = false
        activeValue = ""
        this.settleText()
        this.build()
        return (this.inputTid())
    }

    fn removeValue:void (v:string) {
        def at:int (indexOf values v)
        if (at >= 0) {
            remove_index values at
        }
    }

    ; Focus leaving the input with a query pending: revert or clear. Called by
    ; the host when focus goes to another controller, and by a Tab.
    fn commitBlur:void () {
        if autocomplete {
            if open {
                this.autoClose()
            }
            return
        }
        if (filtering == false) {
            return
        }
        def typed:string input.value
        open = false
        activeValue = ""
        if (multiple == false) {
            if ((strlen typed) == 0) {
                ; Emptied and left: the selection goes with the text. Measured.
                value = ""
            }
        }
        this.settleText()
        this.build()
    }

    ; --- autocomplete mode ------------------------------------------------------
    ; See the header. The filtering, the highlight walk (`moveHighlight`,
    ; `firstEnabled`) and the tree are shared with the combobox above; what
    ; differs is that the text is the value.

    fn autoClose:void () {
        open = false
        activeValue = ""
        if (inlineComplete && (input.value != typed)) {
            ; A completion that was only shown goes: what was typed stays.
            this.putText(typed)
        }
        this.build()
    }

    ; The box shows `t` with the caret at its end.
    fn putText:void (t:string) {
        input.setValue(t)
        input.caret = (strlen t)
        input.anchor = input.caret
    }

    ; A suggestion taken: its label is the text now.
    fn accept:string (v:string) {
        def i:int (this.indexOfValue(v))
        if (i < 0) {
            return ""
        }
        def it:UiItem (itemAt items i)
        if it.disabled {
            return ""
        }
        typed = it.name
        this.putText(it.name)
        open = false
        activeValue = ""
        this.build()
        return (this.inputTid())
    }

    fn autoActivate:string (target:string) {
        if (target == (this.inputTid())) {
            ; openOnInputClick is off: a click places the caret, no more.
            return (this.inputTid())
        }
        if (target == (this.triggerTid())) {
            if open {
                this.autoClose()
                return (this.inputTid())
            }
            open = true
            activeValue = ""
            this.build()
            return (this.inputTid())
        }
        if (target == (this.clearTid())) {
            typed = ""
            this.putText("")
            open = false
            activeValue = ""
            this.build()
            return (this.inputTid())
        }
        def iv:string (this.itemValueOf(target))
        if ((strlen iv) > 0) {
            return (this.accept(iv))
        }
        return ""
    }

    ; The text changed (a key, or the platform's own edit). `was` is the query
    ; before it. The list opens on any text and closes on none; the highlight
    ; is dropped unless an inline completion puts it on the row it completes.
    fn autoEdited:void (was:string) {
        typed = input.value
        activeValue = ""
        open = ((strlen typed) > 0)
        if (inlineComplete && open && ((strlen typed) > (strlen was)) && (input.caret == (strlen typed))) {
            def vis:[UiItem] (this.visibleItems())
            def low:string (to_lowercase typed)
            def n:int (strlen typed)
            def i:int 0
            while (i < (array_length vis)) {
                def it:UiItem (itemAt vis i)
                if (it.disabled == false) {
                    if ((strlen it.name) >= n) {
                        if ((to_lowercase (substring it.name 0 n)) == low) {
                            activeValue = it.value
                            ; The typed letters as typed, the rest of the label
                            ; after them, selected.
                            input.setValue((typed + (substring it.name n (strlen it.name))))
                            input.anchor = n
                            input.caret = (strlen it.name)
                            i = (array_length vis)
                        }
                    }
                }
                i = (i + 1)
            }
        }
        this.build()
    }

    ; The caret or the selection moved and the text did not. With an inline
    ; completion showing, moving off it keeps it: the shown text is the query.
    fn autoCaretMoved:void () {
        if (inlineComplete && (input.value != typed) && (input.hasSelection() == false)) {
            ; Kept as the suggestion spells it, not as the first letters were
            ; typed: "ty" completed and kept is "TypeScript".
            if ((strlen activeValue) > 0) {
                def lab:string (this.labelOf(activeValue))
                if ((to_lowercase lab) == (to_lowercase input.value)) {
                    input.setValue(lab)
                }
            }
            typed = input.value
        }
        this.build()
    }

    ; After an arrow: an inline box shows the highlighted row's whole label.
    fn showHighlighted:void () {
        if (inlineComplete == false) {
            return
        }
        if ((strlen activeValue) == 0) {
            this.putText(typed)
            return
        }
        this.putText((this.labelOf(activeValue)))
    }

    fn autoKey:string (key:string shift:boolean ctrl:boolean) {
        if (key == "Escape") {
            if open {
                this.autoClose()
                return (this.inputTid())
            }
            if ((strlen input.value) > 0) {
                typed = ""
                this.putText("")
                this.build()
            }
            return (this.inputTid())
        }
        if (key == "Enter") {
            if (open == false) {
                return ""
            }
            if ((strlen activeValue) > 0) {
                return (this.accept(activeValue))
            }
            ; Nothing highlighted: the list goes and the text stays.
            this.autoClose()
            return (this.inputTid())
        }
        if ((key == "ArrowDown") || (key == "ArrowUp")) {
            def delta:int 1
            if (key == "ArrowUp") {
                delta = -1
            }
            if ((open == false) && ((array_length (this.visibleItems())) == 0)) {
                ; Nothing to offer: an empty popup is not opened by an arrow.
                return (this.inputTid())
            }
            this.moveHighlight(delta)
            this.showHighlighted()
            this.build()
            return (this.inputTid())
        }
        if (key == "Tab") {
            if open {
                this.autoClose()
            }
            return ""
        }
        def before:string input.value
        def was:string typed
        input.keyDownWith((this.inputTid()) key shift ctrl)
        if (input.value != before) {
            this.autoEdited(was)
        } {
            this.autoCaretMoved()
        }
        return ""
    }

    ; The pointer over a row highlights it — and only that: an inline box's
    ; text follows the keyboard, not the mouse.
    fn hover:string (target:string) {
        if ((autocomplete == false) && (hoverHighlight == false)) {
            return ""
        }
        if (open == false) {
            return ""
        }
        def iv:string (this.itemValueOf(target))
        if ((strlen iv) == 0) {
            return ""
        }
        if ((this.visibleIndexOf((this.visibleItems()) iv)) < 0) {
            return ""
        }
        def it:UiItem (itemAt items (this.indexOfValue(iv)))
        if it.disabled {
            return ""
        }
        if (activeValue != iv) {
            activeValue = iv
            this.build()
        }
        return ""
    }

    ; --- input ----------------------------------------------------------------------

    fn activate:string (target:string) {
        if disabled {
            return ""
        }
        if autocomplete {
            return (this.autoActivate(target))
        }
        if (target == (this.inputTid())) {
            if open {
                return (this.inputTid())
            }
            return (this.openOnChosen())
        }
        if (target == (this.triggerTid())) {
            if open {
                this.closeList()
                return (this.inputTid())
            }
            return (this.openOnChosen())
        }
        if (target == (this.clearTid())) {
            value = ""
            open = false
            activeValue = ""
            this.settleText()
            this.build()
            return (this.inputTid())
        }
        def cv:string (this.chipValueOf(target))
        if ((strlen cv) > 0) {
            ; A click on a chip is a click in the box: the list opens and
            ; focus is the input's. Measured.
            chipFocus = ""
            if open {
                return (this.inputTid())
            }
            return (this.openOnChosen())
        }
        def rv:string (this.chipRemoveValueOf(target))
        if ((strlen rv) > 0) {
            this.removeValue(rv)
            chipFocus = ""
            open = false
            activeValue = ""
            this.build()
            return (this.inputTid())
        }
        def iv:string (this.itemValueOf(target))
        if ((strlen iv) > 0) {
            return (this.choose(iv))
        }
        return ""
    }

    fn typeChar:boolean (target:string ch:string) {
        if (target != (this.inputTid())) {
            return false
        }
        if disabled {
            return false
        }
        input.tid = (this.inputTid())
        if autocomplete {
            def was:string typed
            input.insertText(ch)
            this.autoEdited(was)
            return true
        }
        if (filtering == false) {
            ; The first key turns the label into a query. A resting single box
            ; holds its label with the caret at the end, so the typed letter
            ; lands after it exactly as it does on the reference.
            filtering = true
        }
        input.insertText(ch)
        ; Typing opens the list and drops the highlight. Measured.
        open = true
        activeValue = ""
        this.build()
        return true
    }

    ; The PLATFORM edited the text for us.
    ;
    ; `typeChar` is the door for a host that turns keystrokes into characters
    ; itself. This is the door for one that parks a real `<input>` over the box
    ; and lets the browser do the editing — IME, paste, undo, a phone's
    ; keyboard — and then reports the whole value. The effect on the LIST is
    ; the same either way and is the part a host must not have to reinvent:
    ; typing makes the text a query, opens the list and drops the highlight.
    ;
    ; A report that leaves the text alone is a SELECTION move — a click, a
    ; drag, Ctrl+A — and must not turn a resting label into a query.
    fn applyEdit:boolean (target:string v:string selStart:int selEnd:int) {
        if (target != (this.inputTid())) {
            return false
        }
        if disabled {
            return false
        }
        input.tid = (this.inputTid())
        def before:string input.value
        def wasTyped:string typed
        input.applyEdit(v selStart selEnd)
        if autocomplete {
            if (input.value == before) {
                this.autoCaretMoved()
                return true
            }
            this.autoEdited(wasTyped)
            return true
        }
        if (input.value == before) {
            this.build()
            return true
        }
        filtering = true
        open = true
        activeValue = ""
        this.build()
        return true
    }

    fn keyDownWith:string (target:string key:string shift:boolean ctrl:boolean) {
        if disabled {
            return ""
        }
        input.tid = (this.inputTid())
        def cv:string (this.chipValueOf(target))
        if ((strlen cv) > 0) {
            return (this.chipKey(cv key))
        }
        if (target != (this.inputTid())) {
            return ""
        }
        if autocomplete {
            return (this.autoKey(key shift ctrl))
        }
        if (key == "Escape") {
            if open {
                this.closeList()
                return (this.inputTid())
            }
            ; Escape on a CLOSED single box clears it. Measured, and a
            ; surprise: the second Escape is the clear button's keyboard.
            if (multiple == false) {
                value = ""
                this.settleText()
                this.build()
            }
            return (this.inputTid())
        }
        if (key == "Enter") {
            if (open == false) {
                return ""
            }
            if ((strlen activeValue) > 0) {
                return (this.choose(activeValue))
            }
            ; Nothing highlighted: close, and the query is thrown away — the
            ; single box reverts to its label, the multiple box empties.
            ; Measured; there is no autoHighlight to lean on.
            this.closeList()
            return (this.inputTid())
        }
        if (key == "ArrowDown") {
            return (this.moveHighlight(1))
        }
        if (key == "ArrowUp") {
            return (this.moveHighlight(-1))
        }
        if (key == "Backspace") {
            if (multiple && ((strlen input.value) == 0)) {
                if ((array_length values) > 0) {
                    ; The last chip goes, the list opens, focus stays. Measured.
                    removeLast values
                }
                open = true
                filtering = true
                this.build()
                return (this.inputTid())
            }
            def emptyBefore:boolean ((strlen input.value) == 0)
            if (filtering == false) {
                filtering = true
            }
            input.keyDownWith((this.inputTid()) key shift ctrl)
            if (emptyBefore == false) {
                open = true
                activeValue = ""
            }
            this.build()
            return (this.inputTid())
        }
        if (key == "ArrowLeft") {
            if multiple {
                def atStart:boolean ((input.caret == 0) && (input.anchor == 0))
                if (atStart && ((array_length values) > 0)) {
                    ; Out of the box and onto the last chip; the list closes.
                    ; Measured.
                    open = false
                    activeValue = ""
                    def last:string (itemAt values ((array_length values) - 1))
                    chipFocus = last
                    this.build()
                    return (this.chipTid(last))
                }
            }
            input.keyDownWith((this.inputTid()) key shift ctrl)
            this.build()
            return ""
        }
        if (key == "Tab") {
            this.commitBlur()
            return ""
        }
        ; Everything else is the text field's: ArrowRight, Home, End, Delete,
        ; Ctrl+A, word motion.
        if (key == "Delete") {
            if (filtering == false) {
                filtering = true
            }
        }
        input.keyDownWith((this.inputTid()) key shift ctrl)
        this.build()
        return ""
    }

    ; The arrows on the input: open a closed list, else step the highlight
    ; over the VISIBLE rows, skipping disabled ones, stopping at the ends.
    fn moveHighlight:string (delta:int) {
        def vis:[UiItem] (this.visibleItems())
        if (open == false) {
            open = true
            activeValue = ""
            if (delta > 0) {
                ; Measured on a box with a value: the chosen row. On an empty
                ; one: the first row.
                def chosen:string value
                if multiple {
                    chosen = ""
                    if ((array_length values) > 0) {
                        chosen = (itemAt values 0)
                    }
                }
                if ((this.visibleIndexOf(vis chosen)) >= 0) {
                    activeValue = chosen
                } {
                    activeValue = (this.firstEnabled(vis 0 1))
                }
            } {
                activeValue = (this.firstEnabled(vis ((array_length vis) - 1) -1))
            }
            this.build()
            return (this.inputTid())
        }
        def from:int (this.visibleIndexOf(vis activeValue))
        if (from < 0) {
            if (delta > 0) {
                activeValue = (this.firstEnabled(vis 0 1))
            } {
                activeValue = (this.firstEnabled(vis ((array_length vis) - 1) -1))
            }
            this.build()
            return (this.inputTid())
        }
        def next:string (this.firstEnabled(vis (from + delta) delta))
        if ((strlen next) > 0) {
            activeValue = next
        } {
            if loopFocus {
                ; Off the end and back to the input; the next arrow wraps.
                activeValue = ""
            }
        }
        this.build()
        return (this.inputTid())
    }

    ; The first enabled row at or after `from`, walking by `delta`; "" when
    ; the walk runs off the end. The wrap, when `loopFocus` is on, is the caller's.
    fn firstEnabled:string (vis:[UiItem] from:int delta:int) {
        def i:int from
        while ((i >= 0) && (i < (array_length vis))) {
            def it:UiItem (itemAt vis i)
            if (it.disabled == false) {
                return it.value
            }
            i = (i + delta)
        }
        return ""
    }

    ; Keys while a chip holds focus.
    fn chipKey:string (v:string key:string) {
        def at:int (indexOf values v)
        if (at < 0) {
            return (this.inputTid())
        }
        def n:int (array_length values)
        if (key == "ArrowLeft") {
            if (at == 0) {
                ; Past the first chip and round to the input. Measured.
                chipFocus = ""
                this.build()
                return (this.inputTid())
            }
            def prev:string (itemAt values (at - 1))
            chipFocus = prev
            this.build()
            return (this.chipTid(prev))
        }
        if (key == "ArrowRight") {
            if (at >= (n - 1)) {
                chipFocus = ""
                this.build()
                return (this.inputTid())
            }
            def nxt:string (itemAt values (at + 1))
            chipFocus = nxt
            this.build()
            return (this.chipTid(nxt))
        }
        if ((key == "Backspace") || (key == "Delete")) {
            remove_index values at
            def left:int (array_length values)
            if (left == 0) {
                chipFocus = ""
                this.build()
                return (this.inputTid())
            }
            ; The chip now in its place, or the one before it when it was the
            ; last. Measured both ways.
            def landing:int at
            if (landing >= left) {
                landing = (left - 1)
            }
            def landed:string (itemAt values landing)
            chipFocus = landed
            this.build()
            return (this.chipTid(landed))
        }
        if ((key == "Enter") || (key == "Escape")) {
            chipFocus = ""
            this.build()
            return (this.inputTid())
        }
        return ""
    }

    fn onFocus:void (target:string) {
        def cv:string (this.chipValueOf(target))
        if ((strlen cv) > 0) {
            chipFocus = cv
        } {
            chipFocus = ""
        }
        this.build()
    }

    fn onBlur:void (target:string) {
        chipFocus = ""
        this.commitBlur()
    }

    ; --- the tree -----------------------------------------------------------------

    fn build:void () {
        def word:string (this.stateWord())
        def root:EVGElement (unwrap rootEl)
        root.id = tid
        root.className = "ui-combobox"
        if disabled {
            UiTree.addClass(root "ui-combobox-disabled")
        }
        UiTree.clearChildren(root)

        def group:EVGElement (unwrap groupEl)
        group.id = (tid + "-group")
        group.className = "ui-combobox-group"
        if multiple {
            UiTree.addClass(group "ui-combobox-group-multiple")
        }
        if invalid {
            UiTree.addClass(group "ui-combobox-group-invalid")
        }
        UiTree.setState(group "ui-combobox-group" word)
        UiTree.clearChildren(group)
        UiTree.anchor(group)

        if multiple {
            def chips:EVGElement (unwrap chipsEl)
            chips.id = (this.chipsTid())
            chips.className = "ui-combobox-chips"
            UiTree.clearChildren(chips)
            def i:int 0
            while (i < (array_length values)) {
                def v:string (itemAt values i)
                def chip:EVGElement (UiTree.div((this.chipTid(v)) "ui-combobox-chip"))
                if (v == chipFocus) {
                    UiTree.addClass(chip "ui-combobox-chip-focused")
                }
                def chipTxt:EVGElement (UiTree.label(((this.chipTid(v)) + "-text") "ui-combobox-chip-text" (this.labelOf(v))))
                if (v == chipFocus) {
                    ; A second token on the text, because the sheet matches one
                    ; class per selector and cannot say "text inside a focused
                    ; chip".
                    UiTree.addClass(chipTxt "ui-combobox-chip-text-focused")
                }
                chip.addChild(chipTxt)
                def x:EVGElement (UiTree.div((this.chipRemoveTid(v)) "ui-combobox-chip-remove"))
                UiTree.leafText(x "×")
                chip.addChild(x)
                chips.addChild(chip)
                i = (i + 1)
            }
            group.addChild(chips)
        }

        ; The text box, built by its own controller and then told where it is.
        input.tid = (this.inputTid())
        input.name = name
        input.description = description
        input.disabled = disabled
        input.required = required
        input.invalid = invalid
        if (multiple && ((array_length values) > 0)) {
            ; The placeholder belongs to an EMPTY box, and a box with chips in
            ; it is not empty. The reference's own demo does exactly this.
            input.placeholder = ""
        } {
            input.placeholder = placeholder
        }
        input.build()
        def box:EVGElement (unwrap input.rootEl)
        UiTree.addClass(box "ui-combobox-input")
        if autocomplete {
            ; aria-controls on the box while its list is there — ARIA 1.2
            ; requires it on an expanded combobox.
            box.a11yControls = ""
            if open {
                box.a11yControls = (this.contentTid())
            }
        }
        ; A single box's input IS the box and a theme gives it the width; a
        ; multiple box's input shares the line with chips and stays narrow.
        ; Two tokens, because the sheet matches one class per selector.
        if multiple {
            UiTree.addClass(box "ui-combobox-input-multiple")
            ; The input is the last thing on the chips' line, as in the
            ; reference: inside the wrapping strip, after the last chip, and
            ; onto a line of its own only when that line has no room left. A
            ; sibling of the strip would wrap under the WHOLE strip instead.
            ; Layout only: the rows below give the a11y tree its parents.
            def strip:EVGElement (unwrap chipsEl)
            strip.addChild(box)
        } {
            UiTree.addClass(box "ui-combobox-input-single")
            group.addChild(box)
        }
        ; A spacer, so the clear and the trigger sit at the far edge of a box
        ; whose input has a stated width. Decoration: no id, no role.
        def grow:EVGElement (UiTree.div("" "ui-combobox-grow"))
        group.addChild(grow)

        if (this.showsClear()) {
            def clr:EVGElement (unwrap clearEl)
            clr.id = (this.clearTid())
            clr.className = "ui-combobox-clear"
            UiTree.leafText(clr "×")
            group.addChild(clr)
        }

        if showTrigger {
            def trig:EVGElement (unwrap triggerEl)
            trig.id = (this.triggerTid())
            trig.className = "ui-combobox-trigger"
            UiTree.setState(trig "ui-combobox-trigger" word)
            UiTree.leafText(trig "▾")
            group.addChild(trig)
        }
        root.addChild(group)

        if (open == false) {
            return
        }
        def content:EVGElement (unwrap contentEl)
        content.id = (this.contentTid())
        content.className = "ui-combobox-content"
        UiTree.setState(content "ui-combobox-content" word)
        UiTree.surface(content "bottom" "start")
        UiTree.clearChildren(content)
        def vis:[UiItem] (this.visibleItems())
        if (autocomplete && loading) {
            def ld:EVGElement (unwrap loadingEl)
            ld.id = (this.loadingTid())
            ld.className = "ui-combobox-loading"
            UiTree.leafText(ld loadingText)
            content.addChild(ld)
        } {
            if ((array_length vis) == 0) {
                def em:EVGElement (unwrap emptyEl)
                em.id = (this.emptyTid())
                em.className = "ui-combobox-empty"
                UiTree.leafText(em emptyText)
                content.addChild(em)
            }
        }
        ; Rows go straight into the list, or into their section when they
        ; have one: a section is a box with its heading and then its rows.
        def section:EVGElement content
        def sectionName:string ""
        def j:int 0
        while (j < (array_length vis)) {
            def it:UiItem (itemAt vis j)
            def g:string (this.groupOf(it.value))
            if (g != sectionName) {
                sectionName = g
                if ((strlen g) > 0) {
                    section = (UiTree.div((this.sectionTid(g)) "ui-combobox-section"))
                    section.addChild((UiTree.label((this.sectionLabelTid(g)) "ui-combobox-section-label" g)))
                    content.addChild(section)
                } {
                    section = content
                }
            }
            def el:EVGElement (unwrap it.el)
            el.id = (this.itemTid(it.value))
            el.className = "ui-combobox-item"
            if it.disabled {
                UiTree.addClass(el "ui-combobox-item-disabled")
            }
            if (it.value == activeValue) {
                UiTree.addClass(el "ui-combobox-item-active")
            }
            def itemWord:string "unselected"
            if (this.isChosen(it.value)) {
                itemWord = "selected"
            }
            UiTree.setState(el "ui-combobox-item" itemWord)
            this.itemText(el it)
            section.addChild(el)
            j = (j + 1)
        }
        def more:int (this.hiddenCount())
        if (more > 0) {
            def mo:EVGElement (unwrap moreEl)
            mo.id = (this.moreTid())
            mo.className = "ui-combobox-more"
            UiTree.leafText(mo ((to_string more) + moreSuffix))
            content.addChild(mo)
        }
        root.addChild(content)
    }

    ; A row's label: one run, or — with `emphasis` and a query — three, the
    ; matching letters in the middle one. The runs have no ids, so a click on
    ; any of them is a click on the row.
    fn itemText:void (el:EVGElement it:UiItem) {
        def q:string (this.query())
        def at:int -1
        if (emphasis && ((strlen q) > 0)) {
            at = (indexOf (to_lowercase it.name) (to_lowercase q))
        }
        if (at < 0) {
            UiTree.leafText(el it.name)
            return
        }
        UiTree.clearChildren(el)
        el.textContent = ""
        el.elementType = 0
        def n:int (strlen it.name)
        def e:int (at + (strlen q))
        if (at > 0) {
            el.addChild((UiTree.label("" "ui-combobox-item-text" (substring it.name 0 at))))
        }
        el.addChild((UiTree.label("" "ui-combobox-item-match" (substring it.name at e))))
        if (e < n) {
            el.addChild((UiTree.label("" "ui-combobox-item-text" (substring it.name e n))))
        }
    }

    fn tids:[string] () {
        def a:[string]
        push a tid
        push a (this.inputTid())
        def inner:[string] (input.tids())
        def k:int 0
        while (k < (array_length inner)) {
            def t:string (itemAt inner k)
            if (t != (this.inputTid())) {
                push a t
            }
            k = (k + 1)
        }
        push a (this.triggerTid())
        push a (this.clearTid())
        push a (this.chipsTid())
        def i:int 0
        while (i < (array_length values)) {
            def v:string (itemAt values i)
            push a (this.chipTid(v))
            push a (this.chipRemoveTid(v))
            i = (i + 1)
        }
        push a (this.contentTid())
        push a (this.emptyTid())
        push a (this.moreTid())
        push a (this.loadingTid())
        def gi:int 0
        while (gi < (array_length itemGroups)) {
            def gname:string (itemAt itemGroups gi)
            if ((strlen gname) > 0) {
                if ((indexOf a (this.sectionTid(gname))) < 0) {
                    push a (this.sectionTid(gname))
                    push a (this.sectionLabelTid(gname))
                }
            }
            gi = (gi + 1)
        }
        def j:int 0
        while (j < (array_length items)) {
            def it:UiItem (itemAt items j)
            push a (this.itemTid(it.value))
            j = (j + 1)
        }
        return a
    }

    ; What the HOST may put focus on and route a click through. Wider than
    ; the tab order: the trigger, the clear, a chip's remove and an option are
    ; all tabindex=-1 on the reference, and every one of them hands focus back
    ; to the input as soon as it has acted. `rows()` says which are tab stops.
    fn isFocusable:boolean (target:string) {
        if disabled {
            return false
        }
        if (target == (this.inputTid())) {
            return true
        }
        if (target == (this.triggerTid())) {
            return true
        }
        if (target == (this.clearTid())) {
            return (this.showsClear())
        }
        if ((strlen (this.chipValueOf(target))) > 0) {
            return true
        }
        if ((strlen (this.chipRemoveValueOf(target))) > 0) {
            return true
        }
        def iv:string (this.itemValueOf(target))
        if ((strlen iv) > 0) {
            if (open == false) {
                return false
            }
            def vis:[UiItem] (this.visibleItems())
            if ((this.visibleIndexOf(vis iv)) < 0) {
                return false
            }
            def it:UiItem (itemAt items (this.indexOfValue(iv)))
            return (it.disabled == false)
        }
        return false
    }

    fn rows:[UiRow] () {
        def out:[UiRow]
        def word:string (this.stateWord())

        def inRow:UiRow (UiRow.of((this.inputTid()) (EVGA11yRole.comboBox()) name))
        inRow.state = word
        inRow.disabled = disabled
        inRow.focusable = (disabled == false)
        inRow.tabStop = (disabled == false)
        inRow.hasPopup = "listbox"
        if open {
            inRow.expanded = (EVGA11yTri.yes())
        } {
            inRow.expanded = (EVGA11yTri.no())
        }
        if required {
            inRow.required = "true"
        }
        if invalid {
            inRow.invalid = "true"
        }
        inRow.description = description
        inRow.hasText = true
        inRow.text = input.value
        inRow.placeholder = input.placeholder
        inRow.hasSelection = true
        inRow.selStart = (input.selStart())
        inRow.selEnd = (input.selEnd())
        push out inRow

        if multiple {
            def bar:UiRow (UiRow.of((this.chipsTid()) (EVGA11yRole.toolbar()) ""))
            push out bar
            def i:int 0
            while (i < (array_length values)) {
                def v:string (itemAt values i)
                ; No role, the label as the name, reachable but not a tab
                ; stop — the reference's chip exactly.
                def chip:UiRow (UiRow.of((this.chipTid(v)) (EVGA11yRole.none()) (this.labelOf(v))))
                chip.parentTid = (this.chipsTid())
                chip.focusable = (disabled == false)
                push out chip
                def x:UiRow (UiRow.of((this.chipRemoveTid(v)) (EVGA11yRole.button()) ("Remove " + (this.labelOf(v)))))
                x.parentTid = (this.chipTid(v))
                x.disabled = disabled
                push out x
                i = (i + 1)
            }
        }

        if (this.showsClear()) {
            def clr:UiRow (UiRow.of((this.clearTid()) (EVGA11yRole.button()) "Clear"))
            clr.disabled = disabled
            push out clr
        }

        if showTrigger {
            def trig:UiRow (UiRow.of((this.triggerTid()) (EVGA11yRole.button()) "Open"))
            trig.state = word
            trig.disabled = disabled
            trig.hasPopup = "listbox"
            if open {
                trig.expanded = (EVGA11yTri.yes())
            } {
                trig.expanded = (EVGA11yTri.no())
            }
            push out trig
        }

        if (open == false) {
            return out
        }
        def list:UiRow (UiRow.of((this.contentTid()) (EVGA11yRole.listBox()) ""))
        list.state = word
        if multiple {
            list.multiSelectable = "true"
        }
        push out list

        def vis:[UiItem] (this.visibleItems())
        if (autocomplete && ((array_length vis) > 0) && (loading == false)) {
            ; A list with rows in it is named after its box ("Fruit
            ; suggestions"); an empty or loading one takes its one line of
            ; text as its name instead, below.
            list.name = (name + " suggestions")
        }
        if (autocomplete && loading) {
            ; Collected onto the listbox as its name, as the empty line is.
            def ld:UiRow (UiRow.of((this.loadingTid()) (EVGA11yRole.none()) loadingText))
            ld.parentTid = (this.contentTid())
            push out ld
        } {
            if ((array_length vis) == 0) {
                def em:UiRow (UiRow.of((this.emptyTid()) (EVGA11yRole.none()) emptyText))
                em.parentTid = (this.contentTid())
                push out em
            }
        }
        def more:int (this.hiddenCount())
        if (more > 0) {
            ; Drawn for the eye; a reader is told on the list itself, where it
            ; does not become the list's name.
            list.description = ((to_string more) + " more matches not shown")
            def mo:UiRow (UiRow.of((this.moreTid()) (EVGA11yRole.none()) ""))
            mo.parentTid = (this.contentTid())
            mo.hidden = true
            push out mo
        }
        def sectionName:string ""
        def j:int 0
        while (j < (array_length vis)) {
            def it:UiItem (itemAt vis j)
            def g:string (this.groupOf(it.value))
            def parent:string (this.contentTid())
            if ((strlen g) > 0) {
                parent = (this.sectionTid(g))
                if (g != sectionName) {
                    ; role=group named by its heading, which is then hidden so
                    ; it is not read twice.
                    def sec:UiRow (UiRow.of((this.sectionTid(g)) (EVGA11yRole.group()) g))
                    sec.parentTid = (this.contentTid())
                    push out sec
                    def lab:UiRow (UiRow.of((this.sectionLabelTid(g)) (EVGA11yRole.none()) ""))
                    lab.parentTid = (this.sectionTid(g))
                    lab.hidden = true
                    push out lab
                }
            }
            sectionName = g
            def row:UiRow (UiRow.of((this.itemTid(it.value)) (EVGA11yRole.option()) it.name))
            row.parentTid = parent
            row.disabled = it.disabled
            row.focusable = (it.disabled == false)
            ; `aria-selected` follows the SELECTION, whatever the highlight is
            ; doing. Measured — and the one place this parts from SelectCtl.
            ; An autocomplete has no selection, and marks the highlighted row
            ; instead, as the APG's list-autocomplete example does.
            if (autocomplete && (it.value == activeValue)) {
                row.state = "selected"
                row.selected = (EVGA11yTri.yes())
            } {
            if (this.isChosen(it.value)) {
                row.state = "selected"
                row.selected = (EVGA11yTri.yes())
            } {
                row.state = "unselected"
                row.selected = (EVGA11yTri.no())
            }
            }
            push out row
            j = (j + 1)
        }
        return out
    }
}
